<title>POLAND: Vanstar buys 7.5 pct ComputerLand.</title>
<headline>Vanstar buys 7.5 pct ComputerLand.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S.'s Vanstar Corporation has bought 366,000 shares, or 7.52 percent of shares and shareholder votes in Polish software firm ComputerLand SA, ComputerLand said in a statmement late on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The statement said the deal would help Vanstar provide service to its global clients and lend ComputerLand its expertise in integrating computer systems, which would help the Polish firm attract new clients. It gave no other details.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
